An approximable map out of C that equals the homomorphism recursion of a Tc-algebra is equal to the descent map of that algebra.

Induction on boolean lists shows agreement on structured bottoms and on structured elements. The empty bottom is the case in which the three-way sum on the bottom is the bottom, and a cons step on a bottom rewrites through the successor key and the inductive value. The empty element is the case in which the three-way sum on the terminator is the constant descent value, and a cons step on an element again uses the successor key. Extensionality for maps out of C, on bottoms and on elements, gives the equality.
